Author: Jihong Min <jihongmin63@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 13 05:50:24 2026 +0000

    fix(rewrite): compute two's-complement decode/encode directly, not by looping
    
    `$bitstr_to_int`/`$int_to_bitstr` walked to their result by adding or
    subtracting `2^w` in a loop. That loop makes every slice reaching it
    unprovable for two independent reasons, each measured one-variable on the real
    `$bin_ge` slice: its two correction branches share one head, so their
    dependency pairs share an SCC that admits no linear ranking function (`n` falls
    in one branch and rises in the other, and they cannot actually alternate --
    after `-2^w` the value is at least `-2^(w-1)`, after `+2^w` it is below
    `2^(w-1)` -- but that exclusivity is invisible to the checker); and `Unravel`
    gives each conditional clause its own chain, so k clauses leave k rules sharing
    one lhs, which costs the verdict by itself. Neither lever alone closes the
    slice at budget 300; a 5-rule acyclic probe flips KILLED -> YES 4s when only
    the shared head is split.
    
    Both go away by naming the value instead of walking to it: the result is the
    representative of `n` modulo `2^w`, so one `mod_int` and one correction suffice
    for every `n` -- including the ones the loop needed several passes for (`w = 8,
    n = 600` takes two steps there and one here). Every helper dispatches on a
    computed boolean tag, the idiom `shr` and `Prelude`'s `div_aux` already use, so
    no symbol here has two entry rules.
    
    `w <= 0` still answers 0, and the guard is load-bearing in a new way: the
    closed form alone would answer -1 at `w = 0` (`2^0 = 1`, remainder 0,
    `half = 0`, and `0 >= 0` takes `0 - 1`), turning a divergence into a silent
    wrong value. `To_maude`'s native delegation for this builtin has exactly that
    unguarded shape; it is dead code today because the structural rules are
    declared first, and reviving it needs this boundary fixed too.
    
    Measured (budget 20, serial, one AProVE process per symbol): 13 of the 26 small
    decode-carrying symbols flip TIMEOUT -> YES at 4.3-5.5s, 10/10 previously-YES
    symbols hold, and the 10 large decode-carrying slices sampled stay TIMEOUT
    (761-14,551 rules -- scale, not this poison). Value equivalence against the
    loop checked exhaustively over w = 0..12 with |n| up to 3*2^w+5 (49,276 pairs,
    0 mismatches) plus w = 32/64 spot checks; impty golden byte-identical; the
    interp-vs-Maude result oracle matches on 12/12 spot programs. The execution
    surface changes too (this builtin is not in `delegated_in_native`, so its
    structural rules reach the Maude module): the full-corpus differential and the
    650-symbol termination sweep are running as of this commit.
    
    Probe files, patched slices and the measurement TSVs are under
    `sweeps/itrs-probe/`.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

